# Java 21 — the AMBIENT JVM: what launches sbt, and so what compiles
# everything (in-process dotc). This is not a preference, and it is
# not the whole story any more (jdk26-default-runtime, 2026-09-19) —
# see below for what actually RUNS on.
#
# On JDK 24+ the Security Manager is gone (JEP 486) and with it
# Subject.getSubject, which Hadoop's UserGroupInformation calls on
# every job Spark runs. The failure is
#
#   UnsupportedOperationException: getSubject is not supported
#
# and there is no flag for it: -Djava.security.manager=allow, the
# remedy for 18..23, makes a JDK 26 refuse to start at all. Spark
# 4.2.0's own confirmed range is 17/21/25 (spark-jdk25-guard-fix) —
# nothing here changes that, and okaySpark's own build.sbt settings
# pin its Test/run to 25 regardless of what this file says.
#
# `sdk env install` here, or `sdk env` in a shell that already has it.
java=21.0.7-tem

# TEST/RUN — a SEPARATE knob (jdk26-default-runtime, 2026-09-19):
# build.sbt defaults every module's forked Test/run to the newest GA
# JDK this project has actually verified end to end
# (~/.sdkman/candidates/java/26.0.2.1-tem — 27 is not GA at this date),
# not the ambient one above. Compiling never moves off 21; a released
# service, a `sbt run`, and every test suite but okaySpark's now
# execute on 26 by default. See specs/jdk-compatibility.md.
